  "question": {
    "text": "Reaction $\\mathrm{A}(\\mathrm{g}) \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{~B}(\\mathrm{~g})+\\mathrm{C}(\\mathrm{g})$ is a first order reaction. It was started with pure A<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0003_95cf8416e0f2.png\"/><br />Which of the following option is <u>incorrect</u>?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Initial pressure of A is 80 mm Hg",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The reaction never goes to completion",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Rate constant of the reaction is $1.693 \\mathrm{~min}^{-1}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial pressure of A after 10 minute is 40 mm Hg",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{A}(\\mathrm{g}) \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{~B}(\\mathrm{~g})+\\mathrm{C}(\\mathrm{g})$<br />$\\begin{array}{llll}\\mathrm{t}=0 & \\mathrm{P}_0 & & \\\\ \\mathrm{t} \\rightarrow \\infty & 0 & 2 \\mathrm{P}_0 & \\mathrm{P}_0\\end{array}$<br />$\\begin{aligned} \\mathrm{P}_{\\infty}=3 \\mathrm{P}_0 & =240 \\\\ \\mathrm{P}_0 & =80 \\mathrm{~mm} \\text { of } \\mathrm{Hg}\\end{aligned}$<br />$\\mathrm{Kt}=\\ln \\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{\\infty}-\\mathrm{P}_0}{\\mathrm{P}_{\\infty}-\\mathrm{Pt}}\\right)$<br />$K \\times 10=\\ln \\left(\\frac{240-80}{240-160}\\right)$<br />$\\mathrm{K}=\\frac{\\ell \\mathrm{n} 2}{10}=0.0693 \\mathrm{~min}^{-1}$<br />Option (3) is incorrect"
  }
}